      <div style="margin-top:28px">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#fff;margin:0 0 10px">Compress your CV or resume PDF for job portals</h2>
        <p style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#a1a1aa;line-height:1.75;margin:0">Job application portals and applicant-tracking systems frequently cap CV and resume uploads at 1–2MB, and a single high-resolution photo or designed template can easily push a one-page CV over that limit. Compressing your CV PDF fixes this in seconds without re-exporting from Word or a design tool. Upload your resume, choose Medium compression (or Heavy for the strictest portals), and download — the text stays perfectly sharp so recruiters and automated screening systems read it without issue. Because everything runs locally, your CV with all its personal details is never uploaded to any server.</p>
